WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.091 --> 00:00:03.591
- This is Oshi, a toco toucan,

00:00:04.813 --> 00:00:08.290
the largest and most recognizable
of the toucan family.

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:12.534
They are found throughout
Southern and Central America.

00:00:12.534 --> 00:00:14.680
While their habitat is extensive,

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:17.218
their population has continued to decline

00:00:17.218 --> 00:00:18.968
over the last decade.

00:00:20.344 --> 00:00:22.274
Their appearance is striking,

00:00:22.274 --> 00:00:25.421
with its iconic bill
that covers almost 50%

00:00:25.421 --> 00:00:27.800
of its body surface area.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:31.467
It looks heavy but is
actually rather light.

00:00:32.877 --> 00:00:37.538
They use their bill to pluck
out of reach fruits from trees.

00:00:37.538 --> 00:00:40.493
Toco toucans are considered
extremely gregarious

00:00:40.493 --> 00:00:43.410
and social birds, living in flocks.

00:00:45.581 --> 00:00:48.269
The pet trade and the
destruction of their rainforests

00:00:48.269 --> 00:00:52.019
are the main cause for
decreasing population.

00:00:53.048 --> 00:00:55.048
This is the toco toucan.

